# Gitignored files Orca COPIES into every new worktree (each worktree owns its
# copy). `pnpm worktree:new` does the same thing for worktrees it creates; this
# file is how a worktree created any other way gets the same treatment.
#
# WHY IT MATTERS: without `.env.local` there is no TEST_DATABASE_POOL_URL, so
# every DB-gated suite SKIPS and the #719 precondition test fails. That failure
# is the guard working — a silent skip must never read as a pass.
#
# Literal paths only. Globs are skipped with a warning, so `.env*.local` would
# copy nothing.
#
# DELIBERATELY ABSENT: .env.staging.local and .env.production.local. Those are
# live credentials, and listing them here would put a copy in every worktree.
# Copy one by hand into the single worktree that needs it.
.env.local
